## Everyday commands

> The shims run inside the `sofascore_tools` container automatically.
> Run them from **anywhere inside the repo**. If the container is down they start it
> first (and it has `restart: unless-stopped`, so it survives reboots).

### Container lifecycle (run from this folder, or `make -C ~/Projects/localdev/sofascore-env <t>`)
```sh
make up           # (re)build with the repo's PHP/installer versions + start — run after
                  # the repo bumps PHP (make doctor tells you)
make doctor       # health check: container, PHP version vs repo, APCu/timezone,
                  # composer platform reqs, vendor freshness, test service ports
make down         # stop & remove it
make restart      # recreate it
make build        # rebuild the image
make shell        # interactive bash shell inside the container
make help         # list all targets
```

### Composer
```sh
composer install              # install deps (writes ./vendor)
composer require vendor/pkg   # add a dependency
composer update               # update deps
composer dump-autoload
```

### Static analysis & code style
```sh
composer phpstan              # project config (phpstan-ci.dist.neon)
composer phpstan-editor       # editor config
composer phpstan-shared       # shared-bundle config
composer linter fix           # php-cs-fixer — apply fixes
composer linter fix -- --dry-run --diff   # check only, no changes
composer linter-twig          # twig-cs-fixer
# NOTE: the git pre-commit hook already runs php-cs-fixer on staged files.
# (make phpstan / make cs ARGS="fix" are convenience wrappers for the above.)
```

### Console
```sh
php bin/console <command>     # e.g. php bin/console cache:clear
console <command>             # shim shortcut for `php bin/console`
```

### Tests
```sh
# Bring the 4 test services up on the HOST (uses the repo's compose.test-local.yaml).
# `composer docker:test:up` / `docker:test:down` (what AGENTS.md says) work too: the
# composer shim intercepts them and runs these make targets on the host.
make test-up

composer test                 # full project suite (paratest, ~2446 test files — slow)
composer test-shared          # quick shared suite (~151 unit tests, ~0.1s)
composer test-editor          # editor test suite
composer test -- path/to/SomeTest.php   # a targeted slice

make test-down                # stop the test services when done
make test                     # convenience: test-up + composer test
```

### Sync to the dev server & run the app
```sh
# Option A: VS Code (natizyskunk.sftp, .vscode/sftp.json) uploads each file on save.
#           Branch switches / git pull are NOT uploaded — use Option B after those.
# Option B: from the terminal:
util/toolbox.sh push-changes                   # push your local state to {{ dig "sofascore" "devWorkspace" "SET-data.sofascore.devWorkspace-IN-chezmoi.toml" . }}
util/toolbox.sh push-changes refresh-caches    # + rebuild & pull vendor/var-cache back for the IDE
util/toolbox.sh open-environment               # open the app in the browser

ssh dev                                         # SSH in (also opens the Xdebug reverse-tunnel)
#   cd {{ dig "sofascore" "devWorkspace" "SET-data.sofascore.devWorkspace-IN-chezmoi.toml" . }} && git pull     # update the workspace (agent-forwarded GitHub auth)

# App URL:  {{ dig "sofascore" "appUrl" "SET-data.sofascore.appUrl-IN-chezmoi.toml" . }}
```

### Xdebug
```sh
# WEB:  VS Code Run & Debug -> "Listen for Xdebug (dev server)" (port 9003)
#       + Xdebug Helper browser extension.
#       `ssh dev` must be active (it carries the reverse-forward 44435 -> 9003).
# CLI:  on the dev server, prefix the command with the alias:
#       xdebug bin/console your:command
```

