## Troubleshooting

| Symptom | Fix |
|---|---|
| `zsh: command not found: composer` | Stale shell — `source ~/.zshrc.local` or open a new pane. |
| VS Code format-on-save does nothing | Output panel → "php-cs-fixer". Check `.vscode/settings.json` paths (`make vscode` on a new machine). |
| Files written by the container are root-owned | Shouldn't happen (runs as your UID); if it does, `make down && make up`. |
| `Could not start sofascore_tools. Build it first` | The image is missing (new machine / pruned). Shims never build — run `make up`. |
| Edited `php.ini` but PHP doesn't see it | chezmoi replaces the file, and a single-file bind mount keeps the old inode — `docker restart sofascore_tools`. |
| `make doctor` warns PHP version mismatch | The repo bumped `PHP_VERSION` in its Dockerfile — `make up` rebuilds with it. |
| Xdebug: `remote port forwarding failed for listen port 44435` | Another machine (the Mac) holds the port. Close its `ssh dev`, then reconnect. Only one machine debugs web at a time. |
| ES queries fail right after `make test-up` | Give Elasticsearch a few seconds to become ready. |

---

## Notes / constraints
- **No PHP on the host** — all PHP runs in `sofascore_tools`.
- **The project repo is never modified**; nothing is committed to it. Machine-local config lives in `~/.zshrc.local` (not `~/.zshrc`, which is chezmoi-managed) and in this folder.
- **NetBird** gives direct access to the dev DB/Elastic/etc.; DB clients connect straight to Postgres (no SSH tunnel). SSH itself still goes over the public IP.
- The official SofaScore dev workflow (`{{ dig "sofascore" "setupDoc" "SET-data.sofascore.setupDoc-IN-chezmoi.toml" . }}`) is remote-server-based; this setup keeps that model and only moves the *tooling* into a local container.
